d('butler','Butler aftermath: reaction, religious explanation and mission','Contemporary reception',['Donald Trump','audiences','religious speakers'],'The July 18, 2024 speech narrates spectators believing Trump dead and then recognizing survival. The January 2025 inauguration connects survival to a stated mission.','How does the author\'s Revelation 13:3 comparison distinguish the wound, apparent survival, reported reactions, religious explanation and later political use?','A speaker\'s report of spectators\' thoughts is not a survey. Applause, gratitude, adherence and worship are separate observations.',['butler-speech','inaugural'],['../event-forecast-register/corpus-review/BUTLER-RECEPTION-20240713.md','../reception-history.html'])
d('images','Account publication and the circulation of sacred imagery','Contemporary publication',['Donald Trump','upstream publishers','official accounts'],'The May 2, 2025 account archive records publication of the papal portrait. The merged media register separates this from other publications and sharing relationships.','Who originates an image, which account selects it, what caption is added, and which institution amplifies it?','The first beast, the promoting agent and the image are not the same role. Image content does not measure viewers\' belief. Unverified image descriptions retain their limits.',['pope'],['../event-forecast-register/x-media/index.html','../event-forecast-register/x-media/media-register.json'])
d('authority','Claims about national rescue and legal authority','Contemporary statement',['Donald Trump'],'A February 15, 2025 account post links saving the country to not violating law.','What exception does the maxim suggest, and is a particular later action expressly defended through it?','The post alone identifies neither a case nor a lawful exemption. A claim, an implemented act and a legal ruling require different records.',['law-maxim'],['../event-forecast-register/corpus-review/index.html#r-20250215-law'])
d('food-access','Conditional food access and material dependence','Contemporary statement with qualification',['Donald Trump','benefit recipients','legislators'],'The existing November 4, 2025 record preserves a statement linking SNAP payments to government reopening, alongside the subsequent compliance clarification.','Is the condition imposed on recipients, legislators, distribution institutions or another party, and what actually happens to access?','A financing condition is not automatically a personal-allegiance test. Preserve court orders, exceptions and actual payments before describing a transaction rule.',['snap'],['../event-forecast-register/corpus-review/index.html#r-20251104-snap','../event-forecast-register/ENERGY-SCARCITY-2026-09-16.md'])
d('war-statements','Threats, negotiations and observed military actions','Contemporary statement',['Donald Trump','Iran'],'A July 2018 Twitter statement addresses Iran\'s president and threatens consequences for further threats.','What addressee, trigger, response and interval does the statement specify, and which later events independently establish the outcome?','A threat is not a strike. A treaty or negotiation does not by itself establish deceptive intent or the gathering described in Revelation.',['war'],['../event-forecast-register/truth-social/index.html','../event-forecast-register/corpus-review/index.html'])
d('reagan-survival','An earlier presidential survival-and-return account','Historical comparison',['Ronald Reagan'],'On April 28, 1981, Reagan thanked people for prayers and support, acknowledged others injured, described improved health, and advocated his economic program.','Which parts of the sequence are shared with other public-survival narratives, and which are documented only in one case?','A recurring feature can support a typological question without establishing identical conduct or a unique final fulfillment. No whole-life moral judgment is inferred.',['reagan-return'],['../reception-history.html'])
d('napoleon-reception','Napoleon represented through Revelation 13 in 1808','Historical reception',['Napoleon','Thomas Rowlandson','G. Sauley'],'Princeton catalogues an 1808 etching explicitly applying Revelation 13 imagery to Napoleon.','Which elements did the historical illustrator choose, and how did the image function in its own political setting?','This is direct evidence of a historical comparison being made, not evidence that every depicted analogy was true. The catalogue\'s number associations are not recomputed as identity tests.',['napoleon'])
d('hitler-oath','Institutional loyalty in the 1934 state-official oath','Historical institutional document',['Adolf Hitler','German state officials'],'The August 20, 1934 state-official oath names Hitler as its object of fidelity and obedience while also referring to duties and law.','What changes when an institution attaches loyalty to a named ruler, and how does that differ from a public religious image or ordinary political support?','The source documents a specific oath, not the proposition that every leader with supporters has the same institutional structure. No unsupported claim about who called Hitler Antichrist is added.',['hitler-oath','fascism'])
d('clinton-reception','A reported accusation concerning a magazine cover','Historical reception',['Bill Clinton'],'A 1993 report records readers interpreting Clinton\'s magazine-cover presentation as Antichrist imagery.','What is evidence about an accusation, and what separate evidence would be needed about the person or institution accused?','A hostile interpretation of cover design is not a documented government mechanism.',['clinton-accusation'])
d('obama-reception','An Antichrist claim recorded by a poll publisher','Historical reception',['Barack Obama'],'Public Policy Polling\'s April 2013 page documents that respondents were asked about an Antichrist claim concerning Obama.','What does the existence of the claim establish about reception, as distinct from policy or prophetic identification?','Reported belief is not proof of its object. No result is converted into a politician\'s score or a comparative ranking.',['obama-accusation'])
d('reagan-reception','A documented Antichrist accusation against Reagan','Historical reception',['Ronald Reagan'],'A 1991 court report records an Antichrist accusation against Reagan.','How should an accusation\'s source and setting be preserved before treating it as a precedent?','This record establishes that an accusation was made, not that the accusation was true or representative.',['reagan-accusation'])
d('egypt-kingship','Royal and divine representation in an Egyptian artifact','Historical material culture',['Sahure','divine figure'],'The Met describes a statue joining King Sahure with a divine figure offering life, using royal protection and authority imagery.','Which visual and institutional relationships are comparable, and which depend on a different religion, period or form of government?','Sahure is not identified with Exodus\'s unnamed pharaoh. Sacred kingship is not automatically identical to modern fascism or a contemporary presidency.',['sahure'])
